1":"Official ","52":"OWC specifications","57":"One","49":"Compact adapter with power passthrough","48":"Supports two independent displays through DisplayLink","50":"Buy two separate lightweight portable monitors.","56":" The INVZI Trio Go 16 if you want everything integrated into one portable workstation. The OWC solution if you prefer flexibility in positioning your two monitors."}},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/fallbackMarkdown","o":"replace","v":"What you want is a **three-screen portable workstation**\\: your MacBook Air in the middle, with one monitor on the left and another on the right.\n\nFor your situation, I would look at a dual-screen laptop extender rather than buying two separate monitors.\n\nThere is one important technical requirement: because your MacBook Air supports only one external display natively, the setup needs **DisplayLink compatibility** to run two independent external screens while keeping the MacBook's own screen open. A regular USB-C splitter won't do this. \ue200cite\ue202turn382409search0\ue202turn382409search2\ue202turn382409search7\ue201\n\n## My top recommendations\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn382409product18\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"5:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**1\\. \ue200entity\ue202[\"turn382409product18\",\"INVZI MagHub Trio Go 16\"]\ue201**\n\n(Best integrated travel setup)\n\n# \\$549\n\n- Two 16-inch portable displays\n- Adds two independent screens\n- DisplayLink driver required\n- Approximately 3.88 lb\n- Designed for Mac compatibility\n\nManufacturer compatibility: \ue200url\ue202INVZI compatibility guide\ue202turn507087search4\ue201\\. Weight and pricing: \ue200url\ue202INVZI comparison\ue202turn507087search9\ue201\\.\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn382409product2\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"5:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**2\\. \ue200entity\ue202[\"turn382409product2\",\"INVZI MagHub Dual 15.6\"]\ue201**\n\n# \\$399\n\n- Two 15.6-inch Full HD displays\n- Convenient integrated design\n- No driver needed on supported Macs\n- However, standard M1/M2/M3 MacBooks cannot use both screens independently with the laptop lid open.\n\nThis is not my recommendation unless your Mac supports two native external displays. \ue200url\ue202Manufacturer specifications\ue202turn507087search5\ue201\\.\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn382409product1\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"5:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**3\\. \ue200entity\ue202[\"turn382409product1\",\"OWC Dual HDMI DisplayLink Adapter\"]\ue201**\n\n(Most flexible setup)\n\n# \\$129.99\n\n- Connects two HDMI monitors\n- Supports two independent displays through DisplayLink\n- Compact adapter with power passthrough\n- Buy two separate lightweight portable monitors.\n\nOfficial \ue200url\ue202OWC specifications\ue202turn507087search0\ue201\\.\n\n**My choice\\:** The INVZI Trio Go 16 if you want everything integrated into one portable workstation. The OWC solution if you prefer flexibility in positioning your two monitors.\n\nOne"},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics","o":"remove"},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/appData/opGenui/componentResults/3e979f04-30fe-57ef-933b-57fafb04a40e","o":"add","v":{"status":"resolved","state":{"url":"https://www.owc.com/solutions/usb-c-dual-hdmi-4k-display-adapter-with-power-passthrough?utm_source=chatgpt.com","title":"OWC specifications","source_label":"owc.com","domain":"owc.com","snippet":"\u3010turn507087search0\u3011 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Available data binding: turn507087search0: WebRef[title, domain, url] # USB-C Dual HDMI\u00ae 4K Display Adapter Easily add two HDMI\u00ae displays up to 4K to any Apple M1/...","metadata_label":null,"refid":"turn507087search0","title_before_last_word":"OWC","title_last_word":"specifications"},"safe_urls":["https://www.owc.com/solutions/usb-c-dual-hdmi-4k-display-adapter-with-power-passthr